A Go test, not a separate binary: every tool named in any skill's toolkit_tools must exist in the plugin's MCPToolRegistry.cpp. This is what catches upstream drift when the toolkit is updated.

Spec: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-21-skill-subsystem-design.md section 8.
Agent: unreagent-test-writer.

Toolkit checkout: ../ue-llm-toolkit (Plugin/UELLMToolkit/Source/UELLMToolkit/Private/MCP/MCPToolRegistry.cpp), overridable via the UE_LLM_TOOLKIT environment variable.

Acceptance:
- resolves the checkout via UE_LLM_TOOLKIT, falling back to the sibling path
- t.Skip with a clear reason when the checkout is absent, so CI without it stays green
- failure message names the offending skill AND the unknown tool
- passes against the current 43-tool registry

Depends on #9.
